    "defaultWorkerId": "claude-local",
    "workers": [
      {
        "workerId": "claude-local",
        "kind": "claude-code-cli",
        "command": "C:/Users/murad/.local/bin/claude.exe",
        "args": [
          "--allowedTools",
          "Write(.projectops/execution/*.findings.json),Edit(.projectops/execution/*.findings.json),Write(.projectops/execution/*.effects.json),Edit(.projectops/execution/*.effects.json),Write(.projectops/proof/*.json),Edit(.projectops/proof/*.json)",
          "--setting-sources",
          "project"
        ],
        "notes": "The owner's local Claude Code CLI. Absolute by requirement: a bare name would resolve against the governed checkout before PATH. No credential is passed and no Anthropic API is called — use-anthropic-api remains a forbidden action. The allowlist grants exactly the two records the WORKER owns: its findings and its effects attestation. It deliberately does NOT cover *.brief.json, *.session.json or *.evidence.json — those are ProjectOS's, and a worker able to rewrite the brief it was judged against, or the evidence collected about it, could launder its own run. An earlier grant of .projectops/execution/** was too broad and was narrowed here; `workers.ts` refuses any grant that is not exactly one of the six patterns it enumerates, so a future config cannot widen it silently. The two proof-surface grants were activated for PROJECTOS-AUTONOMOUS-SELF-CHANGE-PILOT1A: `.projectops/proof/*.json` holds no product code, plan, authority record or configuration, and it is the surface that phase's bounded change is made on. `--setting-sources project` was added after PROJECTOS-AUTONOMOUS-SELF-CHANGE-PILOT1A attempt 2: the governed worker loaded the owner's USER-level Claude Code settings, and a user-installed plugin's SessionEnd hook (`node .../session-end-cleanup.mjs`, from the vercel plugin) failed inside Claude Code's own hook shell with `node: command not found`, which made claude.exe exit 1 and the loop read a finished worker as WORKER_REFUSED - a paid gatekeeper call about the owner's plugin list. Restricting the worker to PROJECT settings means nothing the owner installs for their own interactive sessions - plugins, hooks, MCP servers - executes inside a governed run unless it is committed in this repository, which is also the narrower trust boundary. Proven through the adapter's exact exec path: exit 1 with the hook error without the flag, exit 0 with it."
      }
    ]
